  "supportedInput": "Exact authenticated unexpired {runId, jobId}; runId equals batchId; one commit-set reservationSchemaVersion 1 job with exact prebound output transaction and artifact reference, supported files-committed journal and immutable Queue/reservation/destination/commit-set binding.",
  "safetyContracts": [
    "Suggest and bounded-auto require fresh human approval; observe rejects. Global pause permits only this existing-result registration scope while new enqueue remains blocked.",
    "The existing workspace ledger holds typed storage records and grants. Operation-key uniqueness spans enqueue/cancel/storage; generation exposure, images and concurrency exclude storage records.",
    "Consent binds original request hash, run/job IDs, immutable target hash, authenticated client, policy revision and expiry. No caller paths, journal contents, force options, Provider retry or output rewriting authority.",
    "The existing retryGenerationStorage adapter, retryQueueLinkedOutput and OutputWriter.retryFilesCommittedWorkflow register the existing Artifact and finish the same Queue job; no new generation, Provider call, image rewrite, R2 upload or Scene result retry.",
    "Inspection and execution reject cancellation, unknown/lost Provider facts, unsupported state, live lease and active writer. Queue success transaction rechecks current job/lease/attempt/output/reservation and attempt CAS.",
    "If Queue finalization refuses after Artifact registration, existing compensation removes only the newly created registration, preserving result files and other jobs. Startup recovery retains its existing authority to recover prior-process leases.",
    "Queue-owned deferred files-committed journals are excluded from later generic orphan rollback; shared writer transaction ownership covers write/retry/recovery.",
    "Consumed grants never rerun the mutation after unknown outcome. Reconciliation reads exact Queue success plus Artifact lineage; partial or mismatched facts remain unknown. Success acknowledges the goal state, not proof that this command caused it.",
    "Startup preserves only verified Provider-success attempts with exact v1 files-committed snapshot, journal, reservation and inactive writer binding for subsequent output recovery. Generic queued jobs remain unsupported; missing spool, changed reservation and cancelled evidence stay protected."
  ],
